WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.980
I was going to tell you about Tiger Stadium and had the background sound during our broadcast.

2
00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:18.240
We worked very hard, very hard, in creating, in transmitting the sounds of Tiger Stadium to the people who listened on the radio.

3
00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:22.200
Tiger Stadium is a place with a lot of presence,

4
00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:30.220
partially because it’s a bowl and just the way . . . just the way the sound rolls around in that . . . that big edifice.

5
00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:40.160
We made sure, we had parabolic microphones and . . . We just didn’t hang a microphone for crowd noise out of the front window and so forth.

6
00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:40.820
We didn’t do that.

7
00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:44.400
And we had a parabola especially for the band.

8
00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.480
We had the best band pick up of any broadcast network in the country.

9
00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:50.000
And we used the band a lot.

10
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.700
They don’t do that anymore, and I think that’s sad.

11
00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:56.760
The band is a big part of all of this, of the spectacle.

12
00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:04.000
But when we let you hear the band, I mean, it was like the microphone was right in the middle of the 300-piece outfit.

13
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:04.367
Right.

14
00:01:04.367 --> 00:01:07.840
So . . . But we did work at that.

15
00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:12.420
And the reason was, wasn’t that we thought it would just be nice to do that.

16
00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:14.700
It was for a reason, for a purpose.

17
00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:33.460
We wanted you . . . If you were in the Midwest and you were in your car driving along the highway and you just . . . you just were thumbing along looking for something on the radio,

18
00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:34.640
and you would hear this.

19
00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:42.220
Even if nobody was saying a thing, you would recognize the crowd noise and the sound of Tiger Stadium.

20
00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:43.940
We worked on that.

21
00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:52.840
And as a result, we attracted a lot of people throughout the country on that, in that way.

22
00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:57.400
We did have a wide audience, by the way, just getting off into another subject.

23
00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:01.800
We . . . using all those things, we had a very wide audience.

24
00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:06.540
We used to get correspondence from all over the country and overseas and so forth.

25
00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:09.700
A lot of our games were picked up by American Forces Network.
